*======================================================================
* tipi.a99 - TIPISC: find a TIPI, so that DSRLNK never runs its power-up.
* Borrowed from the SAMS Kernel (1.16.1), which found by reading the TIPI's
* DSR ROM that its power-up routine does nothing but pulse the Pi's RESET
* line: run on every disk call, as TXA's DSRLNK does for the cards that
* keep their buffers in VRAM (the engine's picture overwrites them), it
* would restart the Pi each time.  A TIPI is known by its first device
* name, TIPI.  COPYed by the engine's start-up and the workbench's.
*======================================================================
* TIPISC - TIPCRU := the CRU base of a card whose first device is TIPI,
* or 0.  Uses R1-R3, R12.
TIPISC CLR  @TIPCRU
       LI   R12,>1000
TPS1   SBO  0
       CB   @>4000,@HAA        a valid ROM
       JNE  TPS3
       MOV  @>4008,R1          its first device: a length byte and the name
       JEQ  TPS3
       AI   R1,4
       LI   R2,QTIPI
       LI   R3,5
TPS2   CB   *R1+,*R2+
       JNE  TPS3
       DEC  R3
       JNE  TPS2
       MOV  R12,@TIPCRU
TPS3   SBZ  0
       AI   R12,>0100
       CI   R12,>2000
       JL   TPS1
       RT
QTIPI  BYTE 4
       TEXT 'TIPI'
       EVEN
